1
00:00:00,208 --> 00:00:01,501
I thought you were in Cebu?

2
00:00:01,543 --> 00:00:02,751
How did you know?

3
00:00:02,752 --> 00:00:03,962
[JAO] Got any plans tomorrow?

4
00:00:04,003 --> 00:00:04,963
Nope.

5
00:00:05,004 --> 00:00:06,005
[JAO] Good.

6
00:00:06,047 --> 00:00:08,925
[HAN BIN] Are you here to accuse me of more crazy things?

7
00:00:08,967 --> 00:00:10,175
[ARIEL] It’s okay!

8
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:11,385
I like you for Pearl.

9
00:00:11,386 --> 00:00:12,804
I don’t think she likes me.

10
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:13,847
It’s your fault.

11
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:15,849
It’s because you don’t express your true feelings,

12
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,559
you’re always so serious around her.

13
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:19,560
What should I do?

14
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:20,769
[JAO] Are these the mangroves?

15
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:22,689
- [JAO] Amazing. - Ruth, Jao.

16
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:24,231
Hi, Ruth! Nice to meet you.

17
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:26,442
Ruth knows everything about me.

18
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:29,069
I whisper to her all my doubts.

19
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,195
You should try talking to her too.

20
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:31,990
[JAO] She said I should tell you myself.

21
00:00:32,031 --> 00:00:32,824
What is it?

22
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:34,366
I want more than friendship, Kara.

23
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,618
I want to get to know you more.

24
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:36,953
Jao, I’m hard to love.

25
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:38,371
We won’t rush anything.

26
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:40,457
I won’t let you drown.

27
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:41,583
[HAN BIN] Hello!

28
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:42,624
- Hi! - Hi!

29
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:44,127
[GUEST] You look like a K-pop star.

30
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,919
Are you single or taken?

31
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,130
[HAN BIN] I’m single

32
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:48,965
but my heart is already taken.

33
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:51,885
[KARA] The key to good surfing is timing.

34
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:54,763
[JAO] You have to learn how to be one with the waves.

35
00:00:55,513 --> 00:00:56,514
[WOMAN] Jao!

36
00:00:59,934 --> 00:01:01,059
[WOMAN] Jao!

37
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:02,061
Hey!

38
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:03,688
What’s up?

39
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:04,939
[JAO] What are you doing here?

40
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,106
I’m on vacation!

41
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:07,524
Can’t believe I ran into you.

42
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:08,526
I’ve missed you!

43
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:09,944
- Unbelievable. - [WOMAN GIGGLES]

44
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:12,821
Uh, Kara, this is Lexi.

45
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:13,823
- Lexi, Kara. - Hello!

46
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:14,866
-Hi! - Kara.

47
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:16,075
- Lexi. - Jao’s friend.

48
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,744
Nice to meet you!

49
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:19,204
Jao and I go way back.

50
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:20,663
He’s like a brother to me.

51
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:23,291
And this one is like a little sister to me.

52
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:25,167
She’s always traveling by herself

53
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,669
and always on dating apps.

54
00:01:27,003 --> 00:01:29,506
[LEXI] Excuse me! That’s not true! You…

55
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:31,590
- That’s false information! - [JAO LAUGHS]

56
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:33,218
It’s not true!

57
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:35,678
Anyway, where’s Allie?

58
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:39,432
I don’t know.

59
00:01:41,059 --> 00:01:43,645
You don’t know, like, she’s in Manila?

60
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:46,105
Maybe. Or somewhere else.

61
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:48,817
We broke up, Lex.

62
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:50,610
What?

63
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:52,821
No, you’re joking.

64
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:57,617
What?

65
00:01:58,618 --> 00:01:59,911
[LEXI] You broke up?

66
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:12,173
[ALON BY JL]

67
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:26,831
[LEXI] I’m so sorry to hear that.

68
00:03:26,998 --> 00:03:27,999
Are you okay?

69
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:30,043
Have you cried it out? Have you moved on?

70
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:31,251
Are you okay?

71
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:32,253
Slow down.

72
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,297
And I’m very good, actually.

73
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:38,343
It’s just that you and Allie were together for so long.

74
00:03:38,509 --> 00:03:41,095
[LEXI] I mean, I’m sure this is hard for you!

75
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:52,273
But, you know, we all saw this coming.

76
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:54,441
[LEXI] I’m sorry to say this, okay?

77
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:57,362
But Allie’s been very flaky and indecisive.

78
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:58,655
I mean, like…

79
00:03:58,696 --> 00:04:01,407
she keeps leaving and then showing up again.

80
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:05,203
I mean, yeah, you guys look good together, but,

81
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:06,995
honestly…

82
00:04:06,996 --> 00:04:08,998
you two are more like people trying to make it work

83
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,042
than two people who naturally fit.

84
00:04:16,089 --> 00:04:17,507
Actually, you know…

85
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:20,218
it seems like you and Kara have more chemistry!

86
00:04:26,849 --> 00:04:28,476
[LEXI] Okay! Anyway!

87
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:30,227
Enough stressing out.

88
00:04:30,228 --> 00:04:31,145
Let’s move on.

89
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:32,772
I don’t want to talk about Allie anymore.

90
00:04:33,022 --> 00:04:34,607
Good idea.

91
00:04:35,441 --> 00:04:37,151
What about you? How are you?

92
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,069
I’m fine.

93
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:41,781
Enjoying Siargao, enjoying my trip.

94
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:43,992
Do you have friends here?

95
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:45,576
How many days have you been here?

96
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,120
I’m here alone.

97
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:49,038
And I've only been here for two days.

98
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:52,166
I was even planning on staying for another month.

99
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:54,668
There goes the curse.

100
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:56,503
[LEXI GROANS] The curse is real!

101
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:58,506
[LEXI ]I don’t want to leave, I don’t want to go home...

102
00:04:58,548 --> 00:04:59,632
- [KARA LAUGHS] - I don’t want to go back to work…

103
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:01,967
but I have to go back to work. Why do we have to work?

104
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:02,969
I don’t want to work anymore.

105
00:05:03,094 --> 00:05:03,803
Jeez.

106
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:05,220
What do you mean, "curse is real"?

107
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:06,723
I'm sure you met someone here. Right?

108
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:09,684
Seriously?

109
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:14,104
You’ll meet a lot of people here.

110
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:15,522
Just be careful…

111
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:18,151
You don’t want to get your heart broken, right?

112
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:19,944
You know,

113
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:22,487
it's the people Lex meets who should be worried.

114
00:05:22,488 --> 00:05:25,199
You’ve made a lot of men cry, right?

115
00:05:25,241 --> 00:05:28,745
You’re impossible! That’s not true!

116
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:30,287
Those were tears of joy!

117
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:31,788
- Very joyful tears! - [KARA LAUGHS]

118
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:32,790
- Very joyful tears! - [JAO] Oh, please.

119
00:05:33,624 --> 00:05:35,543
Have you gone on a tour yet?

120
00:05:35,918 --> 00:05:37,128
No.

121
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,881
What are you doing on Thursday?

122
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:41,674
Jao and I can show you around.

123
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:43,467
I’m up for it!

124
00:05:43,468 --> 00:05:44,677
Where are we going?

125
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:46,596
We’ll plan it out.

126
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:49,307
- [LEXI] Yay! - [KARA LAUGHS]

127
00:05:49,348 --> 00:05:52,350
- [JAO] So going back to your dating life... - Where would you recommend...

128
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:54,561
[JAO] No, no, no. Don’t change the topic, Lex.

129
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:56,355
- Who did you meet? I know you. - [LEXI] Where’s the best place...

130
00:05:56,397 --> 00:05:58,191
…you’re not leaving because...

131
00:05:58,274 --> 00:06:00,985
- [JAO] Lex would only stay if... - [LEXI LAUGHS]

132
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:16,709
[QUINITO EXHALES CONTENTEDLY]

133
00:06:25,259 --> 00:06:26,469
[HAN BIN] Are you okay, bro?

134
00:06:30,389 --> 00:06:32,100
I got friendzoned, bro.

135
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:36,229
[QUINITO] It’s okay, though.

136
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:39,107
I respect Pearl’s feelings.

137
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:43,986
It’s okay, bro.

138
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:47,240
At least now, you’re free to do other things.

139
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:50,243
And there are lots of pretty girls out there!

140
00:06:50,326 --> 00:06:51,744
Enjoy the island!

141
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,122
You’re right! You’re right, brother.

142
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:57,499
Enjoy the island, that’s what I’m here for.

143
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,126
Not to get my heart broken!

144
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,044
Yeah!

145
00:07:00,045 --> 00:07:02,963
And if you want, I can give you a free tour, free drink.

146
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,799
Whatever you want, just let me know.

147
00:07:05,883 --> 00:07:07,176
Thank you, brother.

148
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:10,847
I’m so happy to have a brother like you in Siargao.

149
00:07:10,888 --> 00:07:11,888
Bro,

150
00:07:11,889 --> 00:07:13,724
we are your family here,

151
00:07:13,891 --> 00:07:15,184
so don’t be sad.

152
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:16,978
Be always happy.

153
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:18,312
- [QUINITO CHUCKLES] - [HAN BIN] Okay?

154
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:20,064
Jao! Join us!

155
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:24,569
Looks like you’re having a serious conversation there.

156
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:27,445
[QUINITO] At least Jao...

157
00:07:27,446 --> 00:07:29,740
always seems happy with Kara.

158
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:31,117
[JAO] Nah.

159
00:07:31,325 --> 00:07:33,035
I’m just a happy guy.

160
00:07:35,371 --> 00:07:37,331
When you first came here,

161
00:07:37,373 --> 00:07:40,167
you were always rushing, checking the time…

162
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:42,295
but now, look at you.

163
00:07:42,461 --> 00:07:43,546
You’re different.

164
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:47,757
[QUINITO] You know, bro...

165
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,594
you and Kara look good together.

166
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,679
What's the status between the two of you?

167
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:54,639
Uh…

168
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,058
we just like...

169
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:58,769
spending a lot of time together

170
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,062
[QUINITO LAUGHS]

171
00:08:01,063 --> 00:08:02,190
Is that "status"?

172
00:08:02,356 --> 00:08:05,567
Well, we’re happy when we’re together

173
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:07,570
and we’re getting to know each other deeper.

174
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:08,612
Oh…

175
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:10,907
- the getting-to-know stage! - [JAO] Yes.

176
00:08:10,948 --> 00:08:12,533
Something like that. [JAO CHUCKLES]

177
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:15,286
But you like Kara, don’t you?

178
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:21,375
I think Kara also likes you.

179
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:23,419
You think so?

180
00:08:23,461 --> 00:08:24,461
Yeah!

181
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:25,463
I mean…

182
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:27,798
she’s happy when Jao is around.

183
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:31,552
And when Jao is away, she’s sad!

184
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:33,971
Really?

185
00:08:34,013 --> 00:08:35,014
Really.

186
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:40,602
- He’s blushing! - [HAN BIN] Look at him!

187
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:43,230
[QUINITO AND HAN BIN LAUGH]

188
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:44,232
[QUINITO] Uh...

189
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:45,566
- Come on, raise your glass, man! - Let’s just drink to that.

190
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:48,193
- Cheers, cheers. - To you and Kara!

191
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,527
- Kara… Jao. - Cheers!

192
00:08:49,528 --> 00:08:50,529
[SIARGAONON] Karajaw!

193
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:53,074
To me and Kara.

194
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:56,327
[HAN BIN EXHALES CONTENTEDLY]

195
00:08:56,369 --> 00:08:58,371
[JAO COUGHS]

196
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,748
- Isn’t it delicious? - This is so strong.

197
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:03,042
- No. - [JAO CLEARS THROAT]

198
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:27,024
Thanks for coming with me on this tour, Ariel.

199
00:09:27,066 --> 00:09:30,736
Anytime, Princess Pearl. Besides, Kara insisted.

200
00:09:31,153 --> 00:09:32,320
[ARIEL] Miss Jen,

201
00:09:32,321 --> 00:09:34,323
- [ARIEL] Miss Isabel, please drink some water! - [PEARL] Oh, here!

202
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:35,574
- [ARIEL] My sister will serve you. - [BYSTANDER] Oh my gosh, he's so hot!

203
00:09:35,616 --> 00:09:36,825
[ARIEL] It’s so hot! It’s so hot in here!

204
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:38,536
- [PEARL] Here! - [ARIEL] But it’s so beautiful, look!

205
00:09:38,577 --> 00:09:39,745
[ARIEL] Wow!

206
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:41,580
What a beautiful view.

207
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:43,666
Princess Pearl!

208
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:45,793
Han Bin oppa!

209
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,588
[ARIEL SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Take a look at that.

210
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:51,215
[ARIEL] Han Bin oppa!

211
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:53,467
[BYSTANDER] He’s hot!

212
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:54,844
Pearl!

213
00:09:54,885 --> 00:09:55,886
I’ll help you!

214
00:09:56,387 --> 00:09:58,388
[BYSTANDER] My bag is heavy, too!

215
00:09:58,389 --> 00:09:59,390
[PEARL LAUGHS]

216
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:02,143
Wow! Your level of freshness is top notch today, Sir Han!

217
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:04,478
[PEARL] Is that a smile or a weapon?

218
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:06,939
Unique level achieved!

219
00:10:08,107 --> 00:10:09,400
- [PEARL] Let’s go? - Let’s go!

220
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:11,444
[ARIEL] Okay, Miss Isabel, Miss Jen,

221
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:12,486
right here, please.

222
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:16,907
This is the beach of General Luna…

223
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:26,667
You’re early.

224
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:29,045
Hi, Kara.

225
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:30,463
I missed you.

226
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,964
[KARA] Hey! Archie!

227
00:10:32,965 --> 00:10:34,299
[KARA] Long time!

228
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,302
When did you get back?

229
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:38,720
Just today. I left my bags at the hotel.

230
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:40,056
- And I came here... - Nice.

231
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:41,473
- to see you. - [KARA LAUGHS]

232
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:43,267
- I’ve missed you so much. - I’ve missed you!

233
00:10:43,309 --> 00:10:44,310
[ARCHIE LAUGHS]

234
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:47,855
[KARA CHUCKLES]

235
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:49,982
[KARA] Uh...

236
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:52,359
Jao, this is Archie.

237
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,569
Archie, this is Jao.

238
00:10:54,987 --> 00:10:55,988
I’m Jao.

239
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:59,116
Archie. Nice to meet you.

240
00:10:59,241 --> 00:11:01,243
Archie’s my friend.

241
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:04,246
He goes back to the island whenever

242
00:11:04,288 --> 00:11:06,582
there are volunteer programs or community works.

243
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:09,418
So, you’re here for vacation?

244
00:11:10,002 --> 00:11:11,420
No, I’m here for Kara.

245
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:13,130
Ah.

246
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:16,801
Y-You guys are…?

247
00:11:17,259 --> 00:11:18,427
Hanging out?

248
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:20,970
Right!

249
00:11:20,971 --> 00:11:22,597
I forgot you have this "No Boyfriend" rule.

250
00:11:22,598 --> 00:11:23,516
- No Boyfriend rule? - I thought you gave that up.

251
00:11:23,517 --> 00:11:24,725
- No Boyfriend rule? - Hey, that’s not true!

252
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,143
- You just made that up! - [ARCHIE LAUGHS]

253
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:27,770
I never had a rule like that!

254
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:29,647
I missed you a lot.

255
00:11:29,688 --> 00:11:31,147
- [KARA LAUGHS] - Haven’t been back in a while.

256
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:33,359
Yeah! You’re just all over the world.

257
00:11:33,609 --> 00:11:35,903
Oh, I heard about your lectures this week.

258
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:36,946
At Farmers?

259
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:38,572
“Lecture” is a bit much.

260
00:11:38,614 --> 00:11:40,116
It’s just a casual workshop.

261
00:11:40,282 --> 00:11:43,994
[ARCHIE] It’s more of a cultural and sustainability immersion.

262
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:45,621
Nice.

263
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:48,707
Noah said you’re helping us out with the immersion.

264
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:51,167
Yeah. He told me about it.

265
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:54,088
Of course, I’ll help with logistics.

266
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:57,382
What do you do, man?

267
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:59,093
Hm? Me?

268
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:01,220
Nothing. Just hanging out.

269
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:02,972
Boring.

270
00:12:03,013 --> 00:12:04,306
[JAO] My life is boring.

271
00:12:04,807 --> 00:12:06,809
No, really. I’m interested.

272
00:12:07,184 --> 00:12:08,601
Uh… I’m on vacation,

273
00:12:08,602 --> 00:12:11,397
so I’m not really interested to talk about work.

274
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:13,607
[ARCHIE SCOFFS]

275
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:15,943
Um...

276
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:18,571
Archie, can I bring Jao along next week?

277
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:20,614
And his friend, too?

278
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:22,283
Yeah, man. Is that okay?

279
00:12:25,661 --> 00:12:28,664
Sure. I’ll text you the schedule of the local immersion.

280
00:13:06,368 --> 00:13:10,288
[ARIEL] This week’s storyteller is Quinito.

281
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:13,000
Let’s go, Storytellers of the Week!

282
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:15,251
My friend is amazing!

283
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:16,337
Right?

284
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:19,548
What made you decide to volunteer today, Quinito?

285
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:22,134
I was just curious. And... you know,

286
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:26,555
I didn’t want my Siargao experience to be just surfing and eating.

287
00:13:26,722 --> 00:13:28,348
And I also want to give back to the kids

288
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:30,643
before I go back to Manila.

289
00:13:31,685 --> 00:13:32,686
Manila?

290
00:13:33,562 --> 00:13:34,772
You’re leaving?

291
00:13:37,525 --> 00:13:39,902
I thought you’re staying here?

292
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,153
[ARIEL SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Exactly!

293
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,031
Um...

294
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:47,284
My friend and I are

295
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:49,703
opening our restaurant in Manila.

296
00:13:50,412 --> 00:13:52,998
This is so sad, Quinito.

297
00:13:54,291 --> 00:13:57,086
Bro, we’re really gonna miss you.

298
00:14:00,297 --> 00:14:02,633
Promise, I’ll be back.

299
00:14:03,842 --> 00:14:04,843
Well…

300
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:07,888
You need a send-off party.

301
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:09,348
[PEARL] There has to be one!

302
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:11,058
Game?

303
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:13,852
[PEARL LAUGHS]

304
00:14:27,032 --> 00:14:28,242
Isn’t Archie amazing?

305
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:29,909
He only used to teach kids.

306
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:31,912
Now he’s running workshops for farmers.

307
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:34,206
Thanks for helping organize all this.

308
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:35,624
No problem.

309
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:37,835
[JAO] Excuse me.

310
00:14:48,470 --> 00:14:50,764
Kara told me you work for Young Horizon?

311
00:14:54,810 --> 00:14:57,896
You won’t stop until you find out what I do for a living, huh?

312
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:01,734
I'm just curious, bro.

313
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:04,403
Why?

314
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:06,697
Are you looking for a new job?

315
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:08,616
[ARCHIE SCOFFS] No.

316
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:10,242
No offense…

317
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:12,786
[ARCHIE] I wouldn’t work for Young Horizon.

318
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:14,120
Excuse me?

319
00:15:14,121 --> 00:15:15,623
Bro, you’re coming off strong.

320
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:17,541
[ARCHIE SCOFFS]

321
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:21,670
I'm just curious if Kara knows what your company is really about.

322
00:15:23,047 --> 00:15:24,256
Do we have a problem?

323
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:26,342
No.

324
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:28,385
No. We’re good.

325
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:35,351
Shall we start?

326
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:38,062
[ARCHIE] Please come in!

327
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:41,190
There’s something wrong with that guy.

328
00:15:43,442 --> 00:15:44,943
I’ll take care of him.

329
00:15:45,235 --> 00:15:46,236
Watch me.

330
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:08,634
We’ve prepared some compost materials,

331
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:10,510
so you guys can try it yourselves.

332
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:12,721
I’ll partner up with Jao.

333
00:16:13,013 --> 00:16:14,682
[JAO] I just find it incredible

334
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:16,057
that the more I get to know you,

335
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:19,520
the more I discover how knowledgeable you are.

336
00:16:19,561 --> 00:16:22,731
And I find your intelligence very attractive.

337
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:24,066
Do you know what that’s called?

338
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:27,277
[LEXI] Which, incidentally, is happening right here, right now?

339
00:16:27,403 --> 00:16:29,405
They got chemistry, bro.

340
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:30,947
Do you like libraries?

341
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:32,449
Yes, Sir Han.

342
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:36,370
You’ve been to all the libraries you mentioned?

343
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:39,415
Someone messaged me, looking for a Song Ji Ho.

344
00:16:39,456 --> 00:16:41,249
- [PEARL] Who’s that? - [ARIEL] I don't know!

345
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:43,252
[JAO] I like seeing you like this, Kara.

346
00:16:43,293 --> 00:16:44,878
I like seeing you happy.

347
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,797
[KARA] I’m happy that you’re here, Jao.

348
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:48,841
I’m thankful you came back.
